    },
    {
      "id": 0,
      "message": "\u003ctg-emoji emoji-id=\"5240241223632954241\"\u003e\u003ci class=\"emoji\" style=\"background-image:url(\u0026#39;//telegram.org/img/emoji/40/F09F9AAB.png\u0026#39;)\"\u003e\u003cb\u003e🚫\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/tg-emoji\u003e India’s IT ministry banned Telegram for one week because some users shared leaked exam questions.\u003cbr/\u003e\u003cbr/\u003eThis punishes \u003cb\u003e150 million\u003c/b\u003e ordinary Telegram users in India — not the insiders who leaked the exam materials.\u003cbr/\u003e\u003cbr/\u003eAnd the ban hasn\u0026#39;t stopped anything. The leaks just moved to other apps.\u003cbr/\u003e\u003cbr/\u003e\u003ctg-emoji emoji-id=\"5348230282140993341\"\u003e\u003ci class=\"emoji\" style=\"background-image:url(\u0026#39;//telegram.org/img/emoji/40/F09F9BA1.png\u0026#39;)\"\u003e\u003cb\u003e🛡\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/tg-emoji\u003e We’ve done a lot to help fix the problem — even though its source is not Telegram.\u003cbr/\u003e\u003cbr/\u003eOver the past few weeks, we removed hundreds of channels sharing leaked exam materials and related scams in India.\u003cbr/\u003e\u003cbr/\u003eWe’ve also been making the “edited” label more visible to prevent backdating scams.\u003cbr/\u003e\u003cbr/\u003e\u003ctg-emoji emoji-id=\"5395335069671910047\"\u003e\u003ci class=\"emoji\" style=\"background-image:url(\u0026#39;//telegram.org/img/emoji/40/F09F8FB3.png\u0026#39;)\"\u003e\u003cb\u003e🏳️\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/tg-emoji\u003e Telegram is a force for good. Banning it — even temporarily — is a mistake.",
